From b4c4f87d2c321d751bb3cb7f34356d5f5eaeba81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini experiment archive <experiment@invalid.example>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 08:27:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] clk: capture native CONN provider shutdown

Pass one stack-owned observation context through the existing state and
disable callbacks. Record the native route, state decision, CONN key,
bus-protection result, five actual control read/store pairs, terminal OFF
condition reads and provider return. Preserve diagnostic reads separately
from the short-circuited condition counters.

Keep native reads, stores, callback order, count-limit faults and returns.
No readback, timeout, retry or recovery operation is added. Existing
non-CONN paths carry an inactive context and direct CONN helpers use NULL.

This unselected native experiment is not an upstream ABI or boot candidate.
The synthetic archive identity supplies no author certification.
